<section id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="kicker">How it works</span>
            <h2>Four steps from terminal to merged branch.</h2>
            <p>No new workflow to learn — fleet sits on top of WezTerm and the tools you already run.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="steps">
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-index">01</div>
                <h3>Pick a project</h3>
                <p>Run <code>fleet</code> from any pane. Choose a project from the list of repos you've added.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-index">02</div>
                <h3>Dashboard opens</h3>
                <p>Fleet splits the window: one pane runs your coding agent, one runs fleet's TUI dashboard beside it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-index">03</div>
                <h3>Dispatch sub-orchestrators</h3>
                <p><code>fleet dispatch "&lt;task&gt;"</code> spins up a background agent in a hidden pane to work a task on its own.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <div class="step-index">04</div>
                <h3>Review, merge, finish</h3>
                <p>Watch activity dots turn from working to done, then merge, optionally push, and clean up from a menu.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
